RentEase — Property Management & Rental Platform

Stack: React, Node.js, Express, MongoDB, Cloudinary, JWT

Core Features:

Property listing with image uploads

Tenant & landlord authentication

Rent payment tracking and due alerts

Maintenance request management

Rating/review system

Dashboard for both tenant & landlord


We’ll cover:

Overall Goal & Tech Stack

Modules / Features Breakdown

Architecture Plan

Development Phases (with timeline)

Feature Priorities (MVP → Advanced)

Tools, Libraries & Integrations

Time Estimate (realistic)

Resume Positioning

🧠 1. Project Goal

A full-stack platform for tenants and landlords to manage rental properties:

Landlords can list, manage, and track rent payments.

Tenants can browse, request, pay, and review.

Both have dashboards showing key info (payments, properties, requests, etc.).

Tech Stack:

Frontend: React.js + Redux Toolkit + TailwindCSS

Backend: Node.js + Express.js

Database: MongoDB + Mongoose

Image Storage: Cloudinary

Auth: JWT + bcrypt

Payments (optional): Razorpay / Stripe (mocked in MVP)

Deployment: Render (Backend) + Vercel (Frontend) + MongoDB Atlas (DB)












🗓 WEEK 1 — Core Setup & Authentication

🎯 Goal: Finish full backend & frontend authentication (tenant/landlord roles).

Day 1 – Setup & Environment

Initialize backend → npm init, install:

express mongoose cors dotenv bcryptjs jsonwebtoken multer cloudinary nodemon


Create folder structure:

/backend
  /config (db, cloudinary)
  /models
  /routes
  /controllers
  server.js


Connect to MongoDB Atlas.

Test sample route /api/test.

✅ Deliverable: Server running, MongoDB connected, one dummy GET route working.

Day 2 – User Model & Auth Routes

Create User model: { name, email, password, role: "tenant"|"landlord" }

Implement:

Register API (hash password)

Login API (JWT return)

Test using Postman.

✅ Deliverable: JWT working and returning on login.

Day 3 – Auth Middleware & Role Protection

Create verifyToken middleware.

Add verifyRole("tenant") / verifyRole("landlord") middleware.

Test protected routes.

✅ Deliverable: Role-based access verified via token.

Day 4 – Frontend Setup (React)

Create frontend → npx create-react-app frontend

Install:

axios react-router-dom reduxjs/toolkit react-redux react-toastify tailwindcss


Setup Tailwind + folder structure.

Add routing:

/login
/register
/dashboard


✅ Deliverable: React app bootstrapped with working routing.

Day 5 – Auth UI + Redux

Create Register/Login forms with validation (formik + yup).

Connect to backend via axios.

Store token + user info in Redux.

Handle redirects after login.

Add toast notifications.

✅ Deliverable: Full authentication system functional end-to-end.

🗓 WEEK 2 — Property Management & Dashboards

🎯 Goal: Build property CRUD + image upload + dashboards for roles.

Day 6 – Property Schema & Routes

Create Property model:

{ title, description, location, rent, ownerId, images[], tenants[] }


Backend routes:

POST /api/properties (landlord only)

GET /api/properties (all)

GET /api/properties/:id

PUT /api/properties/:id (owner only)

DELETE /api/properties/:id (owner only)

✅ Deliverable: Tested CRUD routes via Postman.

Day 7 – Cloudinary Integration

Setup Cloudinary config + multer for image upload.

Update create/edit property routes to handle image upload.

Test single and multiple image uploads.

✅ Deliverable: Property images uploaded and stored in Cloudinary.

Day 8 – Frontend Property Management (Landlord)

Create pages:

MyProperties.jsx (list landlord’s properties)

AddProperty.jsx (create/edit form)

Connect via axios to backend.

Show preview of uploaded images.

✅ Deliverable: Landlord can add, edit, and delete properties.

Day 9 – Frontend Property List (Tenant View)

Create:

PropertyList.jsx → view all available properties.

PropertyDetails.jsx → detail page with images, rent, landlord info.

Add “Request Rent” or “Apply to Rent” button.

✅ Deliverable: Tenant can view and request to rent properties.

Day 10 – Rent Requests / Tenancy Model

Create Tenancy model:

{ tenantId, propertyId, startDate, rentStatus: "Pending"|"Paid" }


Routes:

Tenant: POST /api/tenancies (request rent)

Landlord: PATCH /api/tenancies/:id (approve/reject)

Update dashboard to show active tenancies.

✅ Deliverable: Rent requests flow functional.

🗓 WEEK 3 — Payments, Maintenance & Reviews

🎯 Goal: Build rent tracking, payment management, and maintenance system.

Day 11 – Payment Model & Routes

Create Payment model:

{ tenantId, propertyId, amount, month, status }


Add manual rent payment route (for MVP):
Tenant → /api/payments → marks “Paid”.

✅ Deliverable: Rent payment logic working (manual version).

Day 12 – Payment Integration (Optional Razorpay/Stripe)

Integrate Razorpay (test mode).
Use payment ID & verify signature.

Store transaction in DB.

✅ Deliverable: Real/Mock payment system integrated.

Day 13 – Tenant Dashboard

Components:

Rented Properties

Payment History

Maintenance Requests (table)

API integration for /properties, /payments, /requests.

✅ Deliverable: Tenant dashboard with dynamic data.

Day 14 – Landlord Dashboard

Components:

My Properties

Tenant List (for each property)

Rent Status Overview

Maintenance Requests

✅ Deliverable: Landlord dashboard with all relevant info.

Day 15 – Maintenance Request System

Request model:

{ tenantId, propertyId, issue, status: "Pending"|"Resolved" }


API routes for CRUD.

Tenant UI → Create maintenance request.

Landlord UI → Mark as resolved.

✅ Deliverable: Request system end-to-end done.

Day 16 – Rating & Review System

Review model:

{ tenantId, propertyId, rating, comment }


API endpoints for create/read.

Tenant adds review after payment.

Show average rating on property detail.

✅ Deliverable: Rating system live.

🗓 WEEK 4 — Testing, Optimization & Deployment

🎯 Goal: Make it production-grade and deploy.

Day 17–18 – Validation & Error Handling

Add backend validation (check role before CRUD).

Add centralized error middleware.

Validate frontend inputs via Yup.

✅ Deliverable: Stable backend with proper validation.

Day 19–20 – UI Polish

Add responsive layouts (Tailwind).

Add skeleton loaders/spinners.

Improve empty state UIs and toasts.

✅ Deliverable: UI looks clean and professional.

Day 21 – Notifications (Optional Enhancement)

Add rent due reminders using:

Node cron job

Nodemailer for email alerts (mock)

Display in dashboard as “Rent Due” badges.

✅ Deliverable: Notification system ready (optional).

Day 22–23 – Testing & QA

Test every route with Postman.

Validate flows:

Login → Add Property → Tenant Request → Payment → Review.

Fix any bugs and UI mismatches.

✅ Deliverable: Stable, bug-free version.

Day 24 – Deployment

Host backend on Render or Railway.

Frontend on Vercel.

MongoDB on MongoDB Atlas.

Set environment variables properly (.env).

✅ Deliverable: Live production build online.

Day 25 – Documentation & Resume Prep

Create README.md:

Overview

Tech Stack

Features

Setup Instructions

Screenshots

Write summary for resume + LinkedIn project section.

✅ Deliverable: Full production-grade project, portfolio ready.

🚀 After Finishing MVP

Add bonus features to make it stand out:

Rent due email scheduler (Nodemailer + cron)

Charts in dashboard (Recharts)

Activity logs (“X tenant paid rent on …”)

Search & filter for properties

Role-based analytics (total rent collected, etc.)
